course: dictionary
lesson: 13174
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Franchise is a good example. «The burger franchise opened a second shop in our town» is about a business. «The new franchise has three films and two games» is about a series of stories with the same characters.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about shops or companies, franchise probably means a business that runs with permission from a company. If it is about films, games or books, it means a series. If it is about voting or history, it means the right to vote. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Clue words are your best friends. In «The team owners wanted to sell the franchise», the words team and owners tell you it is a professional sports team. Find the clue words around the hard word, then choose the meaning that fits them.
fact: Franchise is a noun, and it can also be a verb, as in «They franchised their cafe to new owners.»
fact: A franchise can be permission from a company to sell its products or run a shop using its name.
fact: A franchise can be a series of films, games, books or toys based on the same characters.
fact: In formal language, a franchise is the right to vote in elections.
fact: In US sport, a franchise is a professional sports team.
exercise: «The burger franchise opened a second shop in our town.» What does franchise mean here? | *A shop or business run with permission from a company | A flat, wide roof | A type of lamp | The right to vote in elections
exercise: «The new franchise has three films and two games.» What does franchise mean here? | A small hospital | *A series based on the same characters | A sports team | A school club
exercise: «The new film franchise has three films and a game.» Which clue word tells you franchise is about stories? | the | *films | town | opened
test: «Women won the franchise after many years of campaigning.» What does franchise mean here? | A team that plays in the US | A series of films | A burger shop with a famous name | *The right to vote in elections
test: «The team owners wanted to move the franchise to a new city.» What does franchise mean here? | A shop that sells cakes | *A professional sports team | The right to vote | A set of toys
exam: «The franchise was extended so more people could vote.» What does franchise mean here, and which clue shows it? | *The right to vote, because of the words vote and extended | A sports team, because of the word people | A shop run with permission, because of the word extended | A film series, because of the word more
